# Pressure sensor tests

## PlatformIO native tests

The native suite exercises the deterministic pressure-processing logic without
hardware:

```powershell
& C:\Users\<user>\.platformio\penv\Scripts\platformio.exe test -e native
```

It covers sensor disconnect values, range limits, Kalman initialization and
smoothing, spike detection, filter reset, and a disconnect/recovery sequence.

## ESP32 build

Build the production firmware:

```powershell
& C:\Users\<user>\.platformio\penv\Scripts\platformio.exe run -e esp32dev
```

Build the Wokwi-only firmware with the serial processing-test harness:

```powershell
& C:\Users\<user>\.platformio\penv\Scripts\platformio.exe run -e wokwi
```

## Wokwi automation scenario

Install the Wokwi CLI and authenticate it according to the official
documentation. From the repository root, build first and then run:

```powershell
platformio run -e wokwi
wokwi-cli --scenario wokwi.scenario.yaml
```

The `wokwi` PlatformIO environment enables `WOKWI_AUTOTEST` only for the
simulation firmware. The scenario in [`wokwi.scenario.yaml`](../wokwi.scenario.yaml) checks startup
and drives the same pressure-processing cases as the native suite through a
compile-time serial test harness: first reading, smoothing, disconnected
values, valid and invalid range boundaries, spike detection, threshold
behavior, state preservation, disconnect/recovery, and filter reset. It also
checks that the normal fallback loop continues to produce a spike warning.

The current Wokwi diagram does not provide an API to physically unplug the
BMP180 during this run. The native sequence test covers a reading becoming
disconnected and then recovering without corrupting the filter state.

References:

- [PlatformIO unit testing](https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html)
- [PlatformIO GitHub Actions integration](https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/integration/ci/github-actions.html)
- [Wokwi automation scenarios](https://docs.wokwi.com/wokwi-ci/automation-scenarios)
